  "full_text": "Okay, so I did a comic. This is Moses talking to God. We need iron for swords. God says steel. This is, you know, they have magical realism. This is God realism, except it's fiction. So I made a bunch of Moses comics as offerings. I told them not to worry that we're outnumbered two to one because you're with us. You'll lead the charge, right? That's God talking to Moses. We saw a treasure ship on the bottom of the Red Sea. Can you part it again? The Egyptians saw it too. Can I hang out with you all day? You'll start flaming. Okay, so this is the latest one. That's kind of a dumb joke. Anyway, I'm going to delete it. It sucks. It's not, I'm not going to put it on my distribution. But anyway, so now we go to God and get my reward. That's what you're supposed to do with this operating system. Make a comic or make a hymn and then go get your reward. The Bible says, He has compassed me with his net. Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard. I cry aloud, but there is no judgment. He hath fenced up my way that I cannot pass, and he hath set darkness in my paths. He hath stripped me of my glory and taken the crown from my head. he hath destroyed me on every side I am gone my hope he removed like a tree so I did a dumb joke this kind of you have wrought iron fences and I'm kind of explaining you're probably smarter than me but this reminds me of iron compasses anyway so it was a dumb joke so you do a better joke and then God will talk",
